def vtb_infobasket_seasons(
    tag: Optional[str] = "vtb",
    *,
    return_parsed: bool = True,
    return_as_pandas: bool = False,
    **kwargs,
) -> Union[pl.DataFrame, pd.DataFrame, Dict]:
    """Season END year -> season-level CompID for a competition tag (the table every season-keyed wrapper maps with).

    Endpoint: ``GET https://org.infobasket.su/Comp/GetSeasonsForTag``
    Example URL: https://org.infobasket.su/Comp/GetSeasonsForTag?format=json&tag=vtb

    Args:
        tag: Competition tag scoping the profile: vtb (VTB United League, default), vtbyouth, wbc, wpremier or rfb. The season table is read for this tag.
        return_parsed: parse the payload through parse_vtb_infobasket_seasons -> polars DataFrame (default True). Pass return_parsed=False for the raw JSON Dict.
        return_as_pandas: with return_parsed, return a pandas DataFrame instead of polars.
        **kwargs: Forwarded to the underlying HTTP getter.

    Returns:
        A polars/pandas DataFrame by default; the raw JSON ``Dict`` when ``return_parsed=False``.

    Raises:
        NoDataError: The host answered 404 -- the requested resource does not exist. The host has nothing for the request (an empty list, a league the API does not know, a season with no rows).
        AssetFetchError: The fetch failed (a non-2xx answer or a connection failure after retries, e.g. 401/403/429/5xx, or an empty or unreadable 200 body) -- the answer is unknown, not empty. The fetch failed or the answer is unknown or partial: an error envelope or string (HTTP 200), a game that is not final, a partial or possibly truncated page, or a body for another game, person, team, competition, league or season than the one asked for.
        ValueError: The host answered 400 / 422 -- the request is wrong; retrying cannot help. A season the competition tag does not have, or an argument that is not an integer id.

    Example:
        Quick start::

            from sportsdataverse.basketball.vtb import vtb_infobasket_seasons
            vtb_infobasket_seasons()

        See Also:
            * `VTB United League`_ - the league site whose backends these wrappers read
            * `hoopR`_ - SportsDataverse men's basketball package (R)

        .. _VTB United League: https://www.vtb-league.com/
        .. _hoopR: https://hoopR.sportsdataverse.org

    Notes:
        * Owner flag (sdv-internal-refs/vtb/README.md): the VTB United League is run from Russia and several clubs are owned or sponsored by sanctioned state companies (the KHL precedent); Infobasket is the Russian basketball federation's stats platform. Fetching on your own machine is fine; any published data release, hosted mirror or redistribution needs owner (sanctions / legal) sign-off first. No accounts or payments are involved.
        * Unofficial and unsupported: both hosts are keyless public JSON backends of vtb-league.com. No terms of use are published; robots.txt is a 404 on api.vtb-league.com and org.infobasket.su (no rules; vtb-league.com disallows only /wp/wp-admin/). The runtime waits at least 1 s before every request, retries included, and honours Retry-After on 429 / 503. No key, cookie or proxy is used (live-verified direct from the droplet 2026-10-12).
        * Seasons are END years (2026 = 2025-26) on both backends. Infobasket keys everything by competition id: vtb_infobasket_seasons maps the END year to the season-level CompID, and the season-keyed wrappers do that mapping for you. CompID means three things: a season (50714), a stage below it (50720 regular season, 54281 playoff; stage-level wrappers take the stage id from vtb_infobasket_comp_issue) and, in the player season stats, an END year.
        * Ids: the v2 matchId is the Infobasket GameID, the v2 teamId the Infobasket TeamID and the v2 venueId the Infobasket ArenaId. team_id is the key on every team route; comp_team_id (a registration in one stage) and the club-record id of the team page are other key spaces. person_id is one person across clubs and seasons.
        * Errors are HTTP 200: an unknown id answers {MessageType, Message}, an unknown game the string 'BadRequest'; both are AssetFetchError (a failed fetch), never an empty frame. A body for another game, person, team, competition or season than the one asked for is AssetFetchError too, as is a game that is not final (box score, plays and header need GameStatus 1) and a partial GetTeamStats page. An empty list is NoDataError.
        * Coverage: calendars and box scores from 2009-10; play-by-play and shot x/y from 2022-23 only (earlier games give an empty pbp frame), officials in the line-ups from 2022-23. Shot x/y are decimetres from the basket centre (orientation unverified). Counting statistics are null instead of 0 on the wire (the parsers fill 0), percentages and averages are comma-decimal strings (the parsers return floats), the paint statistics are broken and dropped, and dates come in three encodings (the parsers return ISO strings; .NET instants as Moscow time with its +03:00 offset).
        * Personal data: the runtime removes licence numbers, contact and operator-account fields for everyone and the birth dates, birth years and ages of coaches, referees and other officials from every body (also with return_parsed=False). Players' public bio (birth date, height, weight, nationality) is kept.
        * Stage CompIDs: the team routes (TeamRoster, TeamStats, TeamGames) also accept a stage CompID; pass it as params={'compId': 50720} instead of season. Other tags (vtbyouth, wbc, wpremier, rfb) answer through the tag argument; only vtb was captured.
    """
    _caller_params = kwargs.pop("params", None) or {}
    _params = {
        "format": "json",
        "tag": tag,
    }
    _params.update(_caller_params)
    raw = _get(
        "https://org.infobasket.su/Comp/GetSeasonsForTag",
        params=_params,
        **kwargs,
    )
    if return_parsed:
        return parse_vtb_infobasket_seasons(raw, return_as_pandas=return_as_pandas, columns=_PARSER_COLUMNS["seasons"])
    return raw


